title: Proposition 24
---
order: 24
---
short_label: VI.24
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In any parallelogram the parallelograms about the diameter are similar both to the whole and to one another.
----
proof:

Let *ABCD* be a parallelogram, and *AC* its diameter, and let *EG* and *HK* be parallelograms about *AC.*

I say that each of the parallelograms *EG* and *HK* is similar both to the whole *ABCD* and to the other.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="350" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.24 diagram" src="propVI24.gif"/></noscript>
